<title>INDIA: India eases rule on foreign equity in mining.</title>
<headline>India eases rule on foreign equity in mining.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Indian cabinet said on Friday foreign equity stakes of up to 50 percent in the mining sector will be automatically approved.  </p>
<p>A government statement said foreign equity stakes of up to 50 percent in mining would be automatic except in the areas of gold, silver, diamond and precious stones.</p>
<p>In 1993, India opened up the mining of 13 minerals, previously reserved for the state sector, to private firms.</p>
<p>It also invited private investment and greater participation in the mining sector.</p>
<p>But before Friday's announcement, the government had insisted that it approve foreign stakes of up to 50 percent on a case-by-case basis.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi +91-11 301 2024</p>
